# Component placement (Elementplan)

A generator reads a component in its own local axes. Write `placement`, `parameters`, `clearances` and `connections` so the placed object lands where a planner expects it, without reading generator code. The schema (`elementplan-data-schema`, `ComponentPlacement`) holds the same rules.

## Axes

- The origin is the back-left corner of the component.
- **Left and right** are as seen standing in front of the component, facing it. A WC with its transfer area on the left has `side: left`, seen from the room.
- `width` runs along the host wall from left to right, `depth` away from the wall into the room, `height` upwards from the underside.
- All lengths are metres. A length may instead name one of the component's own `parameters` (`width: depth`); it resolves to the value chosen for the placed instance. Never name a parameter the component does not define.

## Host

| `host` | Means | `edge_kinds` |
|---|---|---|
| `floor` | Free-standing; back is the side it faces away from | omit |
| `wall_face` | Back against one wall | required |
| `wall_corner` | Back against one wall, one side against a second | required |
| `wall_opening` | Cuts a wall, belongs to both rooms | required |

- `wall_corner`: `width` runs along the back wall. An L-shaped component adds `width_2` for the leg along the side wall.
- `wall_opening`: the front is the room that declares the opening. Doors (including gates, passages and French windows) size the opening with `clear_width` and `clear_height`. Windows use `width` and `height`.

## Placement fields

- `side_distance_min`: minimum distance from each side that does not stand against a wall to the nearest perpendicular wall. It has no effect on the wall side of a `wall_corner`.
- `axis_spacing_min`: minimum distance between the centre lines of two neighbouring placements of the same component id. Use it for repeated fixtures (urinals, showers, washbasin rows).
- `elevation`: underside above finished floor. Omit it for 0. For a `wall_opening` it is the sill; point it at a `sill_height` parameter when the sill varies.
- All values are ≥ 0.

## Clearances

- `side` names the side the rectangle touches: `front` (room side), `back` (wall side), `left`, `right`, `swing`.
- `width` runs along the touched side, `depth` away from it.
- `offset` shifts the centre along the touched side. Positive is to the right for `front`, `back` and `swing`, towards the front for `left` and `right`. Omit it for a centred clearance.
- `swing` is the door leaf sweep into the room that declares the opening. Every hinged door has one; sliding doors, gates without a leaf and passages do not.
- Clearances may overlap each other but not walls or other components.

## Mirroring

A generator may mirror any component left to right. `left` and `right` clearances swap, offsets along `width` change sign, and a `wall_corner` component takes its side wall on the other side. Write one-sided components (WC transfer area, single bed, examination couch) in one hand only; do not add a mirrored copy.

## Connections

- `max_distance_to_shaft`: straight-line plan distance from the component centre to the nearest shaft edge. Give it for `drainage`; omit it for media that run freely (power, cold water).

## Check

```bash
python ../elementplan-data-schema/scripts/validate_reference.py . components
```

It rejects negative lengths, malformed parameter names, wall hosts without `edge_kinds`, and lengths that name an unknown parameter.
